{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "module": "ES2022",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "strict": true,
    "types": ["bun-types"],
    "outDir": "dist",
    "rootDir": ".",
    // The codebase imports siblings as `./qa-utils.ts`, which bun resolves
    // natively. Without this, every such import is a TS5097 error — 21 of
    // them the moment anything outside `src/` enters the program.
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true
  },
  // `include` used to be `["src/**/*.ts"]` alone, so `tsc --noEmit -p .`
  // typechecked `src/` plus only what `src/` transitively imports: 6 of the
  // 69 files in `content/pipeline`, and not `schemas/types.ts` at all. A
  // green `tsc` therefore said nothing about most of the pipeline — including
  // the block-kind exhaustiveness assertion in `schemas/types.ts`, which
  // cannot fail if it is never compiled.
  //
  // `schemas/**` is in scope now — it is clean, and it is where the block-kind
  // exhaustiveness assertion lives. Widening it here immediately caught a
  // ReferenceError shipped in 958c29e: seven constraint checks had their `ctx`
  // parameter renamed to `_ctx` during a lint drain while their bodies still
  // read `ctx.dir` / `ctx.fileExists`. That commit claimed "`tsc --noEmit` …
  // clean", which was true and meaningless, because the file was not in the
  // program.
  //
  // `content/**` is in scope now too, drained to zero (bean
  // `folio-assistant-tsca`). Adding it here is the point of the drain: the
  // 63 pipeline files nothing in `src/` imports were never compiled, and that
  // is how `validate.ts` shipped a `ReferenceError` and how six bibliography
  // entry points sat dead — importing `../../schemas/references`, a path that
  // does not exist here — without anything reporting it.
  //
  // `scripts/**` is in scope now too, drained to zero. Its 15 errors were not
  // typing nits: `computeStats(paperDir, contentRoot)` was called with ONE
  // argument from two scripts, and both read `conjectures.with_lean_file` and
  // `conjectures.percent_class_axiomatized`, neither of which existed — so the
  // README and the authors' note were interpolating `undefined`.
  //
  // `adapters/**` is in scope now too, drained from 81 to zero. Its errors
  // were not typing nits: 38 catch blocks referenced an `e` binding a lint
  // drain had stripped (a ReferenceError each, all mine, shipped in 958c29e),
  // `resolveOutline` had never existed, and `--http` mode used the SDK's NODE
  // transport for a Bun `Request`.
  //
  // Every tree is now compiled. A green `bun run typecheck` finally means what
  // it says.
  //
  // `test/health/**` is in scope, and the rest of `test/**` deliberately is
  // not. The health sweep is ordinary program code that ships behind a
  // workflow, so a green `typecheck` has to mean something about it. The rest
  // of `test/` is `test/results/` — 500-odd committed JSON verdicts, not
  // program code — plus the Playwright `*.e2e.ts` specs and their `support/`
  // fixtures, matched by `**/*.e2e.ts` and compiled by Playwright's own
  // pipeline; pulling those in here would put a second typechecker over files
  // that already have one, and a disagreement between the two is a failure
  // with no owner.
  //
  // This said `tests/health/**` until 2026-09-19 (bean `auap`), when the two
  // test trees were consolidated onto `test/`. The narrow glob is what keeps
  // the distinction intact across that move: `test/**` would have quietly
  // widened the program to the e2e specs.
  //
  // THE SIBLING INSTANCES WERE OUTSIDE THE PROGRAM, and the comment above said
  // "Every tree is now compiled" while four of them were not. `detangle/` (folded into cat-harness 2026-09-23),
  // `large-datasets/`, `who-iris/`, `who-style-guide/`, `folio-assistant-sci/`,
  // `agent-skills/` and `folio-assistant-core/` are staged top-level instances
  // of THIS repository, so their TypeScript is this repository's TypeScript.
  //
  // It was not a theoretical gap: `detangle/scripts/kg-detangle.ts` carried a
  // live TS2322 (an `EdgeAuthority` table annotated with two of its three
  // values) that tsc could not see, found 2026-09-20 by a review reading the
  // include list rather than trusting a green run.
  //
  // Same `test/` and `*.e2e.ts` reasoning as above applies to each, which is
  // why these are per-directory globs rather than a bare `*/**/*.ts`.
  "include": ["cat-harness/src/**/*.ts", "cat-harness/schemas/**/*.ts", "cat-harness/content/**/*.ts", "cat-harness/scripts/**/*.ts", "cat-harness/skills/**/*.ts", "cat-harness/adapters/**/*.ts", "cat-harness/test/health/**/*.ts", "cat-harness/types/**/*.d.ts", "tools/**/*.ts", "folio-assistant-core/schemas/**/*.ts", "large-datasets/schemas/**/*.ts", "large-datasets/scripts/**/*.ts", "who-iris/scripts/**/*.ts", "who-iris/schemas/**/*.ts"],
  "exclude": [
    // `block-qa-schema` publishes to npm and owns its compiler settings. Its
    // `tests/` are excluded here for a reason that is NOT tidiness (bean `om30`):
    // `tests/parity.test.ts` imports `vitest`, that package's own
    // devDependency, installed into its nested `node_modules` by
    // `check:published-packages`. A runner reaching `tsc --noEmit` has no such
    // install, so this typecheck FAILED with TS2307 — and had done for as long
    // as the step existed, unseen, because `bun test` failed first and Actions
    // stops a job at its first failing step.
    //
    // So nothing CI ever had is lost here: that file has never been typechecked
    // successfully on a runner. It typechecks in a developer container only
    // because another gate's install happens to be present.
    //
    // The package cannot cover it either: its own config emits npm declarations
    // with `rootDir: js` and `emitDeclarationOnly`, and the test additionally
    // wants node types, `allowImportingTsExtensions` and `import.meta.dirname`
    // — Bun-isms that config exists to reject (measured, 5 errors). Adding
    // `vitest` to THIS manifest was the alternative and is worse: a whole test
    // framework and a second runner at the root, for one file's types.
    //
    // RESIDUAL GAP, stated rather than closed: that test file is now typechecked
    // by nothing. Closing it is the package owner's call — a `tsconfig.test.json`
    // carrying those options, run from its own `scripts.test`.
    "cat-harness/schemas/block-qa-schema/tests","dist", "node_modules"]
}
